WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:05.529
Ready Player One, Steven Spielberg's adaptation
of Ernest Cline's bestselling novel, has finally

00:00:05.529 --> 00:00:06.939
arrived in theaters.

00:00:06.939 --> 00:00:10.799
From its dazzling opening sequence to its
epic final battle, the film is absolutely

00:00:10.799 --> 00:00:13.860
packed with decades upon decades of pop culture
references.

00:00:13.860 --> 00:00:17.990
But while some are just fun Easter eggs, others
actually serve a plot function in the grand

00:00:17.990 --> 00:00:18.990
finale.

00:00:18.990 --> 00:00:23.440
We're here to sort it all out as we explain
the ending of Ready Player One.

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:25.560
The ultimate video game showdown

00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:29.920
For Ready Player One's finale, only the biggest
pop culture-packed showdown would do.

00:00:29.920 --> 00:00:34.150
So Parzival — also known by his real name
of Wade Watts — takes action, putting out

00:00:34.150 --> 00:00:38.030
an open call for help to the entire world,
setting the stage for the ultimate battle

00:00:38.030 --> 00:00:41.210
inside the virtual universe known as the OASIS.

00:00:41.210 --> 00:00:45.520
Taking place on Planet Doom from the Voltron
cartoons, the battle involves everyone from

00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:49.400
the Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles to Chucky
himself, who goes on a murder spree perhaps

00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:51.010
unmatched in his own franchise.

00:00:51.010 --> 00:00:55.579
And after the evil Nolan Sorrento summons
MechaGodzilla to assist him, he's taken down

00:00:55.579 --> 00:01:01.290
by Daito, who pilots the iconic RX-78-2 Gundam
from Mobile Suit Gundam after being dropped

00:01:01.290 --> 00:01:04.330
off on the planet by Serenity from Firefly.

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:05.570
Perhaps the best part?

00:01:05.570 --> 00:01:09.729
Just as the evil I-Rock is about to kill the
good guys, Sho takes him out using the ultimate

00:01:09.729 --> 00:01:12.439
'80s weapon — the glaive from Krull.

00:01:12.439 --> 00:01:13.439
Nice.

00:01:13.439 --> 00:01:14.579
A magic spell

00:01:14.579 --> 00:01:19.679
The whole battle is staged in order to help
Parzival and his friends get inside Castle

00:01:19.679 --> 00:01:23.999
Anorak, which is covered by a magic spell
summoned by the powerful Orb of Osuvox.

00:01:23.999 --> 00:01:27.850
Luckily, the team has someone on the inside
— Artemis, who is able to take down the

00:01:27.850 --> 00:01:31.119
shield by uttering the magic incantation that
summoned it.

00:01:31.119 --> 00:01:35.950
Here's the kicker: the spell is actually a
quote from from the 1981 fantasy film Excalibur

00:01:35.950 --> 00:01:40.430
known as "The Charm of Making," a spell spoken
by both Merlin and Morgana Le Fay.

00:01:40.430 --> 00:01:41.540
Who knew, right?

00:01:41.540 --> 00:01:44.040
"Have you forgotten the charm of making?"

00:01:44.260 --> 00:01:51.300
(Klingon translation: "South Park's Imaginationland
did it first.")

00:01:51.620 --> 00:01:53.670
The value of an extra life

00:01:53.670 --> 00:01:57.899
Even after the Orb is deactivated and the
battle seemingly lost, Sorrento isn't ready

00:01:57.899 --> 00:01:58.899
to quit.

00:01:58.899 --> 00:02:03.079
Instead, he uses the Cataclyst, an artifact
which unleashes a mega bomb that instantly

00:02:03.079 --> 00:02:05.969
kills every avatar on the entire planet.

00:02:05.969 --> 00:02:08.819
Every avatar except, as it turns out, Parzival's.

00:02:08.819 --> 00:02:09.819
Why?

00:02:09.819 --> 00:02:13.950
Well, earlier in the film, Parzival had won
a bet with the robotic curator of the Halliday

00:02:13.950 --> 00:02:18.950
Journals, an archive that documents all the
pop culture obsessions of OASIS founder James

00:02:18.950 --> 00:02:19.950
Halliday.

00:02:19.950 --> 00:02:23.540
The reward for winning the bet was an old
quarter — which, in classic video game terms,

00:02:23.540 --> 00:02:28.030
could be used for an extra life to keep playing
on an arcade game after you died.

00:02:28.030 --> 00:02:32.370
Thanks to having this extra life, Parzival's
avatar was resurrected, and he was able to

00:02:32.370 --> 00:02:34.719
complete Halliday's final puzzle.

00:02:34.719 --> 00:02:36.010
The original Easter egg

00:02:36.010 --> 00:02:40.860
After all of that trouble to get there, Halliday's
final challenge seems deceptively simple:

00:02:40.860 --> 00:02:46.569
A vintage television, an Atari 2600 console,
and playing the right game in the right way.

00:02:46.569 --> 00:02:49.490
The game is the 1979 classic, Adventure.

00:02:49.490 --> 00:02:53.030
And the trick, which Parzival immediately
understands, is that you're not actually supposed

00:02:53.030 --> 00:02:57.120
to win the game — you're just supposed to
find the Easter Egg hidden inside it.

00:02:57.120 --> 00:03:01.990
It's not just any Easter egg, though — it's
literally the first video game Easter egg,

00:03:01.990 --> 00:03:05.890
as the very term "Easter egg" was coined to
describe the secret message in the game, which

00:03:05.890 --> 00:03:08.840
reads "Created by Warren Robinett."

00:03:08.840 --> 00:03:12.709
A movie about Easter eggs which has an Easter
egg about the first Easter egg?

00:03:12.709 --> 00:03:15.599
Now that's truly meta.

00:03:15.599 --> 00:03:16.980
One last test

00:03:16.980 --> 00:03:20.500
Even after he's won the final key, Parzival's
challenge isn't over.

00:03:20.500 --> 00:03:25.049
The last test comes when Anorak offers Parzival
a contract, telling him all he has to do is

00:03:25.049 --> 00:03:27.590
sign and the OASIS will be his.

00:03:27.590 --> 00:03:31.329
Parzival refuses to sign, though, because
he realizes it's a test — Halliday, played

00:03:31.329 --> 00:03:36.410
by Mark Rylance, had forced his partner Ogden
Morrow, played by Simon Pegg, to sign a similar

00:03:36.410 --> 00:03:39.180
contract and regretted it for the rest of
his life.

00:03:39.180 --> 00:03:42.930
Fittingly, the test is an echo of a similar
morality test that plays out at the end of

00:03:42.930 --> 00:03:47.480
the classic film Willy Wonka and the Chocolate
Factory, from which the plot of Ready Player

00:03:47.480 --> 00:03:48.480
One is borrowed.

00:03:48.480 --> 00:03:50.180
"I said GOOD DAY!!"

00:03:51.920 --> 00:03:53.579
The true Easter egg

00:03:53.579 --> 00:03:58.020
When he completes the third challenge and
passes Anorak's contract test, Parzival is

00:03:58.020 --> 00:03:59.790
indeed granted control of the OASIS.

00:03:59.790 --> 00:04:05.420
But the true prize, represented by a literal
giant glowing egg, isn't money or fame — it's

00:04:05.420 --> 00:04:09.859
Halliday's belief that connecting with real
people in the real world is more important

00:04:09.859 --> 00:04:13.950
than anything you might do in an imaginary
online fantasy world.

00:04:13.950 --> 00:04:18.260
Wade finally comes to agree, which is how
and why he wins in the end.

00:04:18.260 --> 00:04:22.560
The lesson is driven home when Parzival emerges
from the real world to find Halliday's one

00:04:22.560 --> 00:04:25.950
time partner and best friend, Og Morrow, waiting
for him.

00:04:25.950 --> 00:04:30.330
It turns out Morrow had secretly been monitoring
the competition through his own OASIS avatar

00:04:30.330 --> 00:04:34.760
— the curator of the Halliday Journals,
who gave Parzival the extra life he needed

00:04:34.760 --> 00:04:35.760
to win.

00:04:35.760 --> 00:04:40.130
In a symbolic gesture, Wade honors what he's
learned from Halliday by hiring Morrow back

00:04:40.130 --> 00:04:45.580
as an OASIS consultant, finally repairing
the rift that cost Halliday his best friend.

00:04:45.580 --> 00:04:46.810
Taking the leap

00:04:46.810 --> 00:04:50.880
As the new owner of the OASIS, Wade is suddenly
the most powerful person in the world.

00:04:50.880 --> 00:04:55.720
But he uses his powers for good, putting the
lessons he's learned from Halliday into play.

00:04:55.720 --> 00:04:59.450
He and his friends get Sorrento arrested for
ordering the murder of Wade's aunt.

00:04:59.450 --> 00:05:03.820
Then, he orders that the OASIS be shut down
two days a week to force people back out into

00:05:03.820 --> 00:05:04.820
the real world.

00:05:04.820 --> 00:05:09.410
And finally, he does what Halliday couldn't
and kisses the girl, winning Artemis as the

00:05:09.410 --> 00:05:10.840
ultimate prize.

00:05:10.840 --> 00:05:15.270
Because in the end, love is the ultimate Easter
egg.

00:05:15.270 --> 00:05:16.840
Or...something.

00:05:16.840 --> 00:05:17.920
Thanks for watching!

00:05:17.920 --> 00:05:20.440
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:05:20.440 --> 00:05:22.970
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

